.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Animate a single bone in a \fBSprite\fP's current rig\&. 

Use \fBSprite::getBone()\fP after enabling the animation pose\&. \fBBone\fP inherits \fBAnimated\fP scheduling, scripts, easing, waits, pause, cancellation and completion handlers\&. Position and attachment coordinates are parent-relative; rotation is in radians and time is in seconds\&. \fBmoveTo()\fP, \fBrotateTo()\fP and \fBchangeScaleTo()\fP override their channels, starting from the displayed value\&. \fBmoveBy()\fP and \fBrotateBy()\fP add to each fresh clip sample\&. \fBchangeScaleBy()\fP adds a scale delta to each fresh clip sample\&. Completed controls persist\&.

.PP
Height measures bone length and width measures its transverse bounds/capsule\&. Resize keeps child attachment positions proportional while preserving child sizes\&. Scale and flip propagate through descendants\&. Imported bone axes are preserved\&. Initial dimensions come from child connection distances, with unit length for a terminal bone; physical bones use their capsule dimensions\&. centerOffset is the attachment point in the parent frame; changing it adds a displacement from its reference position to the running clip's attachment motion\&.

.PP
Controls run before pose modifiers and IK\&. Final rotations honor explicit limits, limits on a corresponding named \fBPart\fP, configured two-bone IK limits, and rotary limits connecting mapped physical Parts\&. Physical simulation owns dynamic poses; scripted controls supply animation targets\&. Resize updates capsule geometry and joint anchors outside locked solver callbacks\&. Scaling or reflecting a single live physical bone requires disabling animation physics first; use resize for physical dimensions, or \fBSprite\fP flip to reflect the entire physical assembly\&.

.PP
The \fBSprite\fP advances controls automatically, including while its clip is paused\&. Use \fBpauseSchedule()\fP to pause the controls\&. Pose queries never advance their clocks\&. Replacing or disabling the rig invalidates handles\&. \fBisAttached()\fP remains safe; other getters and edits throw after invalidation\&. \fBBone\fP handles and their controls are runtime state and are not included in \fBSprite\fP snapshots\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The \fBSprite\fP must have an enabled animation pose\&. Do not edit controls inside pose modifier callbacks\&. Use the callback's borrowed pose to edit that pose\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const forearm = sprite\&.getBone('forearm');
forearm\&.series()
    \&.rotateBy(0\&.5, 0\&.3, pdg\&.easeInOutQuad)
    \&.wait(0\&.2)
    \&.diminish(0, 0\&.25)
    \&.endSeries();

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::enableAnimationPose()\fP, \fBSprite::getBone()\fP, \fBAnimated\fP 
.RE
.PP

