.SS "\fBBone\fP clearIKLimits ()"

.PP
Remove this \fBBone\fP's explicit limit override\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBBone\fP for chaining\&. Existing \fBPart\fP, IK and physical-joint limits still apply\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBBone\fP diminish (number influence, number seconds, int easing = \fR\fBlinearTween\fP\fP)"

.PP
Ease scripted bone influence back toward the running animation\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Blends controlled channels toward each fresh authored sample\&. Zero releases all controlled channels, including flips\&. This changes scripted influence, not alpha\&. A value between zero and one retains the corresponding fraction of control\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinfluence\fP Finite factor from zero to one\&. 
